-- REM-A7-PLAIN-1 (2026-10-26, charter pillar reach; rem-a7 fork F3; owner card 1000181, owner_prompts op-mvnq2nswe765).
-- The card asks that every paper's plain-language summary avoid jargon and detailed numbers, read at an average adult level, define every technical term inline, and that the paper stay implementable by a
-- domain expert; then that the published papers be audited against those rules and their summaries revised. Delivered with this file's PR: docs/PAPER-AUTHORING-GUIDELINES.md (the four rules made checkable, where each is
-- enforced, the gaps) and the audit of the corpus (living-paper D1, SELECT only, 2026-10-26): 704 published papers, 704 plain summaries; Flesch-Kincaid grade 296 at 8 or below, 356 at 9 or below, 348 above 9, 224 above 12,
-- mean 9.57, worst 24.5; 495 summaries hold six or more digit characters, 5 carry a DOI, arXiv id or et al, 169 had a sentence dropped by the grounding gate at build.
-- The summaries are generated by qnfo-gateway plainPrompt / plainBuild, a file another session holds (ASK-PLAIN) and a summary is never edited by hand, so the generator change and the refill are filed as one issue with a
-- code-task line and a probe on the corpus, and the writer-prompt line for the paper itself as a second small one. Card 1000181 closes as superseded by the first. No cap raised, no gate or probe weakened, nothing deleted.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = (SELECT b.status FROM bak_20261026_rem_a7_plain_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), last_verdict = (SELECT b.last_verdict FROM bak_20261026_rem_a7_plain_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class) WHERE class IN (SELECT class FROM bak_20261026_rem_a7_plain_contracts); UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = (SELECT b.triage_state FROM bak_20261026_rem_a7_plain_triage b WHERE b.issue_id = issue_triage.issue_id), close_evidence = (SELECT b.close_evidence FROM bak_20261026_rem_a7_plain_triage b WHERE b.issue_id = issue_triage.issue_id) WHERE issue_id IN (SELECT issue_id FROM bak_20261026_rem_a7_plain_triage); UPDATE agent_issues SET status = 'open', close_channel = NULL WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM bak_20261026_rem_a7_plain_issues WHERE status = 'open')

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_rem_a7_plain_contracts AS
  SELECT class, issue_id, status, verify_probe, verify_transport, last_verdict
  FROM remediation_contracts
  WHERE class = 'issue-1000181';
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_rem_a7_plain_triage AS
  SELECT issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, close_evidence, reopened_count
  FROM issue_triage
  WHERE issue_id = 1000181;
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_rem_a7_plain_issues AS
  SELECT id, status, close_channel, updated_at
  FROM agent_issues
  WHERE id = 1000181;

-- 1. The doer for the summaries: generator change and refill, with a probe on the corpus
INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'PLAIN-STANDARD-1: 348 of 704 published plain-language summaries are above grade 9 and 224 above grade 12; the summary prompt asks for key numbers and has no comparison or hard grade gate',
  'Charter pillar: reach. Successor of owner card 1000181 (owner_prompts op-mvnq2nswe765): plain-language summaries must avoid jargon and detailed numerical analysis, read at an average adult level, define every technical term inline and leave the paper itself implementable by a domain expert. The standard is docs/PAPER-AUTHORING-GUIDELINES.md (rules R1 to R4, where each is enforced, the audit).' || char(10) ||
  'Measured 2026-10-26 (living-paper D1, SELECT only): 704 published papers and 704 plain summaries; Flesch-Kincaid grade (plain_summary.grade) 296 at 8 or below, 356 at 9 or below, 348 above 9, 224 above 12, mean 9.57, worst 24.5 (a summary of the Majorana zero mode paper); 495 summaries hold six or more digit characters; 5 carry a DOI, arXiv id or et al; 169 had a sentence dropped by the grounding gate at build.' || char(10) ||
  'Cause: plainPrompt in qnfo-gateway/worker.js asks for the claim and its key numbers and for a technical term in one short clause or left out (no comparison); plainBuild keeps the lower grade of at most two tries even when it is above PLAIN_TARGET_GRADE = 9, so half the corpus is above the gate and a third above grade 12.' || char(10) ||
  'Change (qnfo-gateway/worker.js only; the file is held by the ASK-PLAIN work, so take the work claim when it is free, WORK-CLAIM-1): (1) plainPrompt: at most two figures, rounded or in words; no DOI, link, citation marker or et al; every technical term defined once in one clause of everyday words, a short everyday comparison allowed when it adds no fact; sentences under 20 words, for an average adult (about grade 8). (2) plainBuild: when the best candidate is still above a PLAIN_HARD_GRADE of 12, one more pass shortens it to at most two short sentences; a text above 12 is never stored. (3) Record the rule version in plain_summary.method (for example model+ground+v2) so plainFill refills the rows made under the old prompt, worst grade first, within PLAIN_FILL_MAX a run. The grounding and residue gates stay as they are, no new model, no cap change; the refill is about 350 summaries at 12 a run.' || char(10) ||
  'Definition of done: the closing probe on this issue (d1-query@living-paper) reads: no published paper has a plain summary above grade 12 or a DOI, arXiv id or et al in it, at least 75 percent are at grade 9 or below, and every published paper still has a summary.' || char(10) ||
  'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-gateway/worker.js' || char(10) ||
  'code-anchor: function plainPrompt(paper, digest, strict) {',
  'claude-session-rem-a7-f3', 'reach', 'high', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.title LIKE 'PLAIN-STANDARD-1:%' AND a.status = 'open');

INSERT INTO remediation_contracts (class, issue_id, precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, max_attempts, escalate_to, expected_cadence_h, status, next_due_at)
SELECT 'issue-' || a.id, a.id,
  'REM-A7-PLAIN-1: the published plain-language summaries are above the reading and reference rules of docs/PAPER-AUTHORING-GUIDELINES.md',
  'qnfo-code-orchestrator through the code-task line on the issue (qnfo-gateway plainPrompt, plainBuild and the plainFill refill); the probe measures the whole published corpus',
  'WITH p AS (SELECT s.grade, s.text FROM plain_summary s JOIN papers x ON x.slug = s.slug WHERE x.status = ''published''), t AS (SELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM papers WHERE status = ''published'') AS published, COUNT(*) AS with_summary, SUM(grade > 12) AS over12, SUM(grade <= 9) AS le9, SUM(instr('' '' || lower(text) || '' '', '' doi '') > 0 OR instr(lower(text), ''doi:'') > 0 OR instr(lower(text), ''doi.org'') > 0 OR instr(lower(text), ''arxiv'') > 0 OR instr('' '' || lower(text), '' et al'') > 0) AS ref_words FROM p) SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN with_summary >= published AND over12 = 0 AND ref_words = 0 AND le9 * 100 >= with_summary * 75 THEN ''ok'' ELSE with_summary || '' of '' || published || '' published papers have a plain summary: '' || over12 || '' are above grade 12, '' || ref_words || '' mention a DOI, arXiv id or et al, '' || le9 || '' are at grade 9 or below (75 percent needed)'' END AS observed FROM t',
  'd1-query@living-paper', 3, 'qnfo-gateway', 1, 'active', datetime('now')
FROM agent_issues a
WHERE a.title LIKE 'PLAIN-STANDARD-1:%' AND a.status = 'open'
ON CONFLICT(class) DO UPDATE SET issue_id = excluded.issue_id, precondition = excluded.precondition, action = excluded.action, verify_probe = excluded.verify_probe,
  verify_transport = 'd1-query@living-paper', max_attempts = excluded.max_attempts, escalate_to = excluded.escalate_to, expected_cadence_h = excluded.expected_cadence_h,
  status = 'active', last_verdict = NULL, next_due_at = datetime('now');

-- 2. The paper itself (rule R4): one line in the writer prompt
INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'PAPER-AUDIENCES-1: the paper writer prompt never asks for the general, cross-disciplinary relevance of a result in words a non-specialist can follow',
  'Charter pillar: reach. Rule R4 of docs/PAPER-AUTHORING-GUIDELINES.md (owner card 1000181): the main paper stays specific enough for a domain expert to understand and implement, and interpretable enough for a non-expert to see the result general and cross-disciplinary relevance. The writer prompt in qnfo-research-exec/worker.js already opens Section 1 with the real-world problem and names users and readiness in Section 7; it never asks the Introduction to say which other fields or problems the result could matter to.' || char(10) ||
  'Change (one line, qnfo-research-exec/worker.js, next to the line Write for an adjacent-field expert; define jargon once): the Introduction closes with one or two plain sentences naming other fields or problems the result could matter to, each stated only as far as the paper itself supports it. Derivations, parameters and procedure stay exact; no other writer or reviewer prompt changes; a paper that already does this is not rewritten.' || char(10) ||
  'Definition of done: the writer prompt on main carries the line (code-probe below); a new paper read after the deploy has the sentences in its Introduction.' || char(10) ||
  'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-research-exec/worker.js' || char(10) ||
  'code-anchor: "- Write for an adjacent-field expert; define jargon once.",' || char(10) ||
  'code-probe: {"paths": ["qnfo-research-exec/worker.js"], "contains": "PAPER-AUDIENCES-1"}',
  'claude-session-rem-a7-f3', 'research', 'medium', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.title LIKE 'PAPER-AUDIENCES-1:%' AND a.status = 'open');

-- 3. The card: delivered what is delivered here, the rest carried by the issues above
UPDATE remediation_contracts
   SET status = 'superseded', last_verdict = 'superseded:REM-A7-PLAIN-1 (the guidelines are delivered in docs/PAPER-AUTHORING-GUIDELINES.md; the generator change and the corpus audit probe are PLAIN-STANDARD-1)', last_attempt_at = datetime('now')
 WHERE class = 'issue-1000181' AND status IN ('active', 'holding', 'monitoring', 'escalated')
   AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues s WHERE s.title LIKE 'PLAIN-STANDARD-1:%' AND s.status = 'open');

INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence)
SELECT a.id, 'plain-standard:PLAIN-STANDARD-1', 'closed', 'qnfo-gateway', datetime('now'),
  'superseded by ' || s.id || ' (PLAIN-STANDARD-1) for the generator change and the corpus probe, and by ' || w.id || ' (PAPER-AUDIENCES-1) for the writer-prompt line. Delivered here: (1) the guidelines, docs/PAPER-AUTHORING-GUIDELINES.md, with the owner''s four rules made checkable (R1 at most two rounded figures and no reference tokens, R2 Flesch-Kincaid grade 8 target, 9 gate, never stored above 12, R3 each technical term defined once inline with an optional comparison that adds no fact, R4 an exact body plus a plain closing of the Introduction), where each is enforced today and the gaps; (2) the audit of the published corpus, measured 2026-10-26 in living-paper (SELECT only): 704 papers published and 704 plain summaries, grade 8 or below 296, 9 or below 356, above 9 348, above 12 224, mean 9.57, worst 24.5; 495 summaries with six or more digit characters, 5 with a DOI, arXiv id or et al, 169 with a sentence dropped by the grounding gate at build; the cause is plainPrompt asking for key numbers with no comparison and plainBuild keeping the lower of two tries even above the grade 9 gate. Revising the summaries is the refill in PLAIN-STANDARD-1 (qnfo-gateway/worker.js is held by the ASK-PLAIN session; its code-task and a corpus probe, no summary above grade 12 and 75 percent at grade 9 or below, are on that issue); no summary is edited by hand and no paper text is rewritten.'
FROM agent_issues a
JOIN (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'PLAIN-STANDARD-1:%' AND status = 'open' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1) s
JOIN (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'PAPER-AUDIENCES-1:%' AND status = 'open' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1) w
WHERE a.id = 1000181 AND a.status = 'open'
ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = 'closed', owner = excluded.owner, close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence;

-- 4. The decision
INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'rem-a7-f3',
  'a plain-language summary is a generated text keyed on the paper, so revising the published ones is the generator change plus a refill, never a hand edit; the guideline is the checkable form of the owner rules, and a rule with no probe is not a rule',
  'REM-A7-PLAIN-1: docs/PAPER-AUTHORING-GUIDELINES.md added; issues PLAIN-STANDARD-1 (qnfo-gateway code-task, corpus probe on d1-query@living-paper) and PAPER-AUDIENCES-1 (qnfo-research-exec code-task and code-probe) filed; card 1000181 closed as superseded by them',
  'living-paper 2026-10-26 (SELECT only): papers 704 published, plain_summary 704 rows, grade <= 8 296, <= 9 356, > 12 224, mean 9.57; digit characters >= 6 in 495; reference tokens in 5; qnfo-gateway/worker.js plainPrompt, plainBuild, PLAIN_TARGET_GRADE = 9, PLAIN_MAX_SENT = 6 and qnfo-research-exec/worker.js writer requirements read on main; work-locks: qnfo-gateway/worker.js held by claude-code-ask-plain-20261026',
  'applied by migration',
  'one doc added, one line added to docs/ENSEMBLE-POLICY.md; two agent_issues rows opened and one closed; one contract inserted and one superseded; no worker, cron, cap or gate changed',
  'the Rollback line reopens card 1000181 and restores its contract; the two new issues stay open as findings',
  'the owner reading rules for plain-language summaries have a written standard, a corpus probe and a doer',
  'after the generator change and refill the probe reads ok: no summary above grade 12, 75 percent at grade 9 or below; until then PLAIN-STANDARD-1 stays open',
  'reach: summaries a non-specialist can read',
  'd1:living-paper plain_summary and papers (SELECT only); qnfo-gateway and qnfo-research-exec source on main; offline node:sqlite suite migrations/rem-a7-plain.test.mjs'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log d WHERE d.action LIKE 'REM-A7-PLAIN-1:%');
